{"kind":"article","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A kind is a 32-bit number that every record carries. A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of a kind holds the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declared with that kind and no others, so one program can hold your routes, another library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"analytics events and a third’s migrations without any of them seeing the others."}]},{"text":"Choosing the number","type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-the-number","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any number other than 0 works. 0 marks an empty slot, and the macros refuse it. The convention is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"four ASCII letters that name the thing, read as one byte each: “rout” is "},{"code":"r","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"o","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"t","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x72","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x6F","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x75","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"0x74","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the kind is "},{"code":"0x726F_7574","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The letters make it unlikely that two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"libraries pick the same number, and they stay readable in a hex dump of the binary. Swift computes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one for you:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let kind = \"rout\".utf8.reduce(0) { $0 << 8 | UInt32($1) }  \/\/ 0x726F_7574"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Give the kind a name for the code that reads it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that reads the set for its users keeps the name internal: the macro writes the kind as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number, so its users’ files never need it."}]},{"text":"When two libraries pick the same number","type":"heading","anchor":"When-two-libraries-pick-the-same-number","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No compiler sees every module at once, so nothing can check that a kind is unique. If two libraries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"choose the same number, their records land in the same set. A record still hands over its value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only when asked for its own type, so a set of a type your library owns ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Route"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds only your declarations. Read your records as a type of your own, and a clash costs nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the time to skip the other library’s records."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Within a kind, records may share any value. To make two declarations of the same route or event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name fail to build, give each a unique key: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Writing the kind at each declaration","type":"heading","anchor":"Writing-the-kind-at-each-declaration","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" takes the kind as an integer literal. It has to be a literal because the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"macro writes it into the binary at compile time; a named constant isn’t visible to the macro:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That suits a kind used in a few places. A typo in the number puts the declaration in the wrong","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set without any error, though.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Giving your users a macro","type":"heading","anchor":"Giving-your-users-a-macro","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A library that asks its users to register things gives them a macro with the kind built in, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":" and never see the number. The macro lives in a small compiler plugin built on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the LinkerSetsMacroSupport module, whose documentation walks through the plugin, the macro’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration and the package’s targets. The plugin can also require a protocol of every type it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registers, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" on a type that isn’t an event fails to compile where it’s written."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"type":"topic","title":"Unique keys","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"type":"topic","title":"Performance","abstract":[{"text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","kind":"symbol","title":"LinkerSet","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)":{"type":"topic","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declares a record of "},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose value is this declaration’s."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetEntry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt32","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","type":"topic"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","role":"collection"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","role":"article","title":"Finding records","type":"topic"}}}